<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns A to Taegu Metropolitan Government.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns A to Taegu Metropolitan Government.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Ltd (S&amp;P) said on Thursday it had assigned its A long-term issuer credit rating to Taegu Metropolitan City Government (TMG), Republic of Korea.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said the outlook is stable.</p>
<p>Taegu's large capital-expenditure program is likely to restrain the city's rating, unless the expenditure is substantially subsidised by the central government, S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>The Taegu economy, however, may yield substantial future growth and revenues if new automobile manufacturing plants are successfully opened and reinforce other efforts to diversify the economy, it added.</p>
</text>
